# check: fail error[M19g]: 'l' holds a view of 'v' taken before 'v' may have grown
# vec1 review, found beside it: a conversion names its argument's storage (T29a), so "String(v.View())" keeps the view's
# M19g, round 2 (brought back from round 1's deletion): the same Vec is seen on both sides, so the view is refused
# loan - pushed into a List of text it would outlive the buffer the next Push replaces
import "std/io"
fn main() ? {
    v := Vec<Char>()
    v.Push('a')
    l := List<String&>()
    l.Push(String(v.View()))
    for i in range 100 { v.Push('b') }
    try io.Println(l[0])
}
